.TH EGRAPH-BUILD 1 2026-09-29 "egraph @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
egraph-build \- evaluate the installed packages through portage and write egraph's store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B egraph-build
.RB [ \-\-full | \-\-incremental | \-\-evaluate | \-\-json | \-\-evaluated\-json | \-\-pending | \-\-emerge\-options | \-\-notices ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ entry ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B egraph-build
imports portage, read-only, and writes what
.BR egraph (1)
answers from: the installed store (every installed package's dependencies, slots, sonames and the
root sets) and the evaluated store beside it (the dependencies emerge reads, masks, and the
versions each package could move to).
Both are written to temporary files and renamed into place, so readers never see a partial store.
.PP
.B egraph
runs it itself whenever the store no longer describes the system, so it rarely needs running by
hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-full
Evaluate every installed package (the default).
.TP
.B \-\-incremental
Evaluate again only the packages whose inputs changed since the stores were written.
.TP
.B \-\-evaluate
As
.BR \-\-incremental ,
and evaluate each
.IR entry ,
a category/package name with ebuilds in a repository, with what it would pull in.
The evaluated store keeps them through later builds until a
.BR \-\-full
one, or until they are installed.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the installed layer as canonical JSON instead of writing the store.
.TP
.B \-\-evaluated\-json
Print the evaluated layer as canonical JSON instead of writing the store.
.TP
.B \-\-pending
Write what each
.I entry
of a merge list
.RB ( ebuild:\fIcpv\fR " or " binary:\fIcpv\fR )
waits for, as JSON, to
.BR \-\-output .
.TP
.B \-\-emerge\-options
Write
.B EMERGE_DEFAULT_OPTS
as emerge splits it, a word a line, to
.BR \-\-output .
.TP
.B \-\-notices
Write the configuration files with updates waiting, as emerge finds them, and the unread news
items with their titles, as JSON, to
.BR \-\-output .
.TP
.BI \-\-output " file"
The file
.BR \-\-pending ", " \-\-emerge\-options " and " \-\-notices
write, apart from anything portage prints.
.TP
.BI \-\-store " file"
The store to write (default
.BR $EGRAPH_STORE ,
else
.IR ${EROOT}/var/cache/egraph/installed.egraph );
the evaluated store goes beside it.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " dir"
The root whose installed packages to evaluate (default
.BR $ROOT ).
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-root " dir"
The root of the portage configuration to evaluate them with (default
.BR $PORTAGE_CONFIGROOT ).
.TP
.BI \-\-eprefix " dir"
The offset prefix of a prefix installation (default
.BR $PORTAGE_OVERRIDE_EPREFIX ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR ROOT ", " PORTAGE_CONFIGROOT ", " PORTAGE_OVERRIDE_EPREFIX ", " EGRAPH_STORE
Defaults for
.BR \-\-root ", " \-\-config\-root ", " \-\-eprefix " and " \-\-store .
.TP
.B EGRAPH_STRICT
When 1, an incremental build is also compared with a full one, and a difference fails it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure.
.TP
.B 2
The command line could not be parsed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR egraph (1),
.BR portage (5)
